## Phase 3: Magic Link Invite System

### 3.1 Create Invitation Model
**New file:** `backend/internal/models/invitation.go`

```go
type Invitation struct {
    ID          uint       `gorm:"primaryKey"`
    Email       string     `gorm:"not null;index"`
    TokenHash   string     `json:"-" gorm:"not null;uniqueIndex"`
    InvitedByID uint       `gorm:"not null"`
    ExpiresAt   time.Time  `gorm:"not null"`
    UsedAt      *time.Time
}
```

### 3.2 Add Token Functions
**File:** `backend/internal/auth/tokens.go`

- `CreateInvitationToken(db, email, invitedByID)` - 7-day TTL
- `ValidateInvitationToken(db, token)` - check expiry, not used
- `ConsumeInvitationToken(db, token)` - mark used

### 3.3 Add Invitation Handlers
**New file:** `backend/internal/handlers/invitations.go`

- `POST /admin/invitations` - Admin creates invite, returns magic link
- `GET /auth/invitation/:token` - Validate invite (public)

### 3.4 Update Signup
**File:** `backend/internal/handlers/auth.go`

- Accept optional `invite_token` in signup request
- Validate and consume token
- Verify email matches invitation
- Auto-verify email for invited users

### 3.5 Add Routes
**File:** `backend/cmd/server/main.go`

```go
api.GET("/auth/invitation/:token", invitationHandler.Validate)
admin := protected.Group("/admin")
admin.Use(middleware.AdminMiddleware())
admin.POST("/invitations", invitationHandler.Create)
```

### 3.6 Frontend Signup Page
**File:** `frontend/src/app/signup/page.tsx`

- Read `?invite=xxx` from URL
- Call `/auth/invitation/:token` to validate
- Pre-fill email, pass token to signup API

